<reference id="_Toc235450397" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 5 — Image with caption</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an image of the printer's ink tank area wrapped in a &lt;figure&gt; element with</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>locations</keyword>
        <keyword>caption</keyword>
        <keyword>Figure</keyword>
        <keyword>Image</keyword>
        <keyword>figure</keyword>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
        <indexterm>locations</indexterm>
        <indexterm>caption</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider an image of the printer's ink tank area wrapped in a <codeph>&lt;figure&gt;</codeph> element with a <codeph>&lt;figcaption&gt;</codeph> element reading "Figure 1: Ink tank and cap locations".</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Image with caption</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;figure>
  &lt;img src="media/ink_tank_area.png" alt="Ink tank and cap locations"/>
  &lt;figcaption>
    Figure 1: Ink tank and cap locations
  &lt;/figcaption>
&lt;/figure></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;fig>
  &lt;title>Ink tank and cap locations&lt;/title>
  &lt;image href="media/ink_tank_area.png">
    &lt;alt>Ink tank and cap locations&lt;/alt>
  &lt;/image>
&lt;/fig></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The <codeph>&lt;figure&gt;</codeph> wrapper is mapped to a DITA <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph> element. The <codeph>&lt;figcaption&gt;</codeph> text is mapped to the <codeph>&lt;title&gt;</codeph> element inside <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph>. Figure number prefixes such as "Figure 1:" are stripped from the <codeph>&lt;title&gt;</codeph> text during conversion, retaining only the descriptive label.</p>
<note type="note"> Always use the native HTML <codeph>&lt;figure&gt;</codeph> and <codeph>&lt;figcaption&gt;</codeph> elements to add captions to images. A <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element placed above or below an <codeph>&lt;img&gt;</codeph> and used as a visual caption is mapped to a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element, not a <codeph>&lt;title&gt;</codeph>.</note>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
